            <div xml:id="d780">

                <pb facs="0725" n="719" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg719"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1453: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Egypt</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fish</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-03-01T11:00:00+02:00">March 1, 1939—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>23. Department’s 12, February 25, 2 p.m. I called on the Foreign Minister this
                    morning and left with him an <hi rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire</hi> embodying
                    the exact phraseology used in the Department’s telegram No. 9, February <pb
                        facs="0726" n="720" xml:id="pg720"/> 21, 1 p.m., paragraph 1. Copies of the
                    correspondence and statement mentioned therein were attached to the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">aide-mémoire.</hi></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fish</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
